    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d758">

                <pb facs="0795" n="745" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg745"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr.
                            Terrell.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Department of
                                State</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1894-10-29"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 29,
                    1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your No. 320<anchor n="1" xml:id="d758-f1"/> received. Your untenable demand that
                    native teachers in American schools be not arrested without your consent may
                    have been due to misapprehension of my telegram of 3d instant. While you will
                    protest against capricious or unreasonable arrest of such persons as occasion
                    requires you will not insist the Government of the Porte shall agree in advance
                    that it will not arrest its own subjects for violating its own laws without your
                    consent.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
